figdown 0.1 block
# `RULE-POSITION-ENUMERATION`: RULE 2.4's enum half is language-wide, not
# surface-wide — the two experimental enum positions are `extend=` on a
# `band` and `type=` on a `chart`.
# 0.3 (`SCENE-KEYWORD-MEMBERSHIP`): the first section declared `figdown 0.1 topology` until
# this release, and `band` was WITHDRAWN from that genre — in a topology
# document a BAND is a frequency band. This fixture is one of the two
# occurrences the withdrawal cites: both were conformance fixtures, never a
# figure anyone needed. The section is REWRITTEN to `block`, which is the
# genre that still declares `band`, rather than deleted — the subject is
# `extend=`'s enum position, not the genre it was written under. Both
# messages are unchanged by the move; only their line numbers shift, with
# this comment.
node a "A"
band "Zone" 15% in=a extend="up"
figdown 0.1 table
table t "T"
| A | B |
|---|---|
| 1 | 2 |
chart t type="bar3d"
